# Based on the "Andrea, Brad, Carter, Delilah" worked example from Wikipedia's
# "Counting single transferable votes" article (2 seats, 4 candidates, 57 voters).
#
# Note: the article computes its quota as a plain 57/(2+1)=19, without the "+1" of the
# standard Droop quota; this tool implements the standard formula, floor(v/(s+1))+1=20.
# The article also only gives round-by-round *totals*, not individual ballots, so the
# ballot-level breakdown here is reconstructed (not copied from a source) to reproduce
# those totals under the standard quota. First preferences: Andrea 40, Delilah 17,
# Brad 0, Carter 0 (adjusted from the article's 39/17/0/0, which sum to 56, not 57).
4 2
24 1 2 0
16 1 3 2 0
17 4 0
0
"Andrea"
"Brad"
"Carter"
"Delilah"
"Andrea, Brad, Carter, Delilah (adapted from Wikipedia)"
